      "dom_id": "question-37456",
      "problem": "The function \n$f(x,y)$ \nhas the second derivative\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(1,1).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $H(1,1)>0$\n- $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)>0$\n- The point $(1,1)$ is a local minimum of $f$",
      "worked_solution": "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(1,1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the determinant of $\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=det(\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(1,1))=2\\cdot 0-{1}^{2}=-1<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)=(\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(1,1))_{11}=2>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $H(1,1)<0,$ then $(1,1)$ is a saddle point by the second partial derivative test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "html": "<div id=\"question-37456\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">58.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/1944#12585\">Classifying a Critical Point Using the Second Partial Derivatives Test</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"37456\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>The function \n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1731\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D453 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> \nhas the second derivative\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1732\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\" style=\"color: red;\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5C\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c62\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6F\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6C\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c64\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c79\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6D\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c62\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6F\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6C\"></mjx-c></m